1.bug_scenario:
When formatting a switch statement with an inline comment on the `case` and `default` labels, Prettier 2.3.2 preserves the comment after the colon on a `case`, but for the `default` branch it moves the `// comment` onto its own line below the `default:`. The screenshot shows:

  switch (peek_keyword()) {
    …
    default: // expression;
      return ExpressionStatement.read();
  }

being reformatted to:

  default:
    // expression;
    return ExpressionStatement.read();

instead of keeping the `// expression;` on the same line as `default:`.
